itter\nL177: \nL178: cite11†Sarah Key ^{  cite12†1 }, cite13†Peter G Ryan ^{  cite14†2 }, cite15†Sarah E Gabbott ^{  cite16†3 }, cite17†Jack Allen ^{  cite12†1 }, cite18†Andrew P Abbott ^{  cite19†4 }\nL179: \nL180: Affiliations Expand\nL181: ### Affiliations\nL182: \nL183:   * ^{1} School of Chemistry, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK.\nL184:   * ^{2} FitzPatrick Institute of African Ornithology, University of Cape Town, Rondebosch 7701, South Africa.\nL185:   * ^{3} School of Geography, Geology and the Environment, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK.\nL186:   * ^{4} School of Chemistry, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK. Electronic address: apa1@le.ac.uk.\nL187:   * PMID: 38432345\nL188:   * DOI: cite20†10.1016/j.envpol.2024.123701†doi.org L189: Free article\nL190: \nL191: Item in Clipboard\nL192: # Influence of colourants on environmental degradation of plastic litter\nL193: \nL194: Sarah Key et al. Environ Pollut. 2024.\nL195: \nL196: Free article\nL197: \nL198: Show details\nL199: \nL200: Display options\nL201: \nL202: Display options\nL203: \nL204: Format [Select]\nL205: \nL206: [Button: Environ Pollut ]\nL207: \nL208: Actions\nL209: \nL210:   * cite9†Search in PubMed L211:   * cite10†Search in NLM Catalog†www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov L212:   * cite3†Add to Search L213: \nL214: . 2024 Apr 15:347:123701.\nL215: \nL216: doi: 10.1016/j.envpol.2024.123701. Epub 2024 Mar 1.\nL217: ### Authors\nL218: \nL219: cite11†Sarah Key ^{  cite21†1 }, cite13†Peter G Ryan ^{  cite22†2 }, cite15†Sarah E Gabbott ^{  cite23†3 }, cite17†Jack Allen ^{  cite21†1 }, cite18†Andrew P Abbott ^{  cite24†4 }\nL220: ### Affiliations\nL221: \nL222:   * ^{1} School of Chemistry, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK.\nL223:   * ^{2} FitzPatrick Institute of African Ornithology, University of Cape Town, Rondebosch 7701, South Africa.\nL224:   * ^{3} School of Geography, Geology and the Environment, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK.\nL225:   * ^{4} School of Chemistry, University of Leicester, Leicester, LE1 7RH, UK. Electronic address: apa1@le.ac.uk.\nL226: \nL227:   * PMID: 38432345\nL228:   * DOI: cite20†10.1016/j.envpol.2024.123701†doi.org L229: Item in Clipboard\nL230: \nL231: [Button: Full text links ]Cite\nL232: \nL233: Display options\nL234: \nL235: Display options\nL236: \nL237: Format [Select]\nL238: ## Abstract\nL239: Plastic degradation and the resultant production of microplastics has an important effect on the environment and fauna across the world. This paper shows that the colourant incorporated into plastic formulations has a significant effect on the stability of plastics.\nL240: A static experimental exposure of differently coloured polypropylene bottle tops from the same manufacturer to a moderate climate over 3 years showed that black, white and silver plastics were almost unaffected whereas the specific blue, green and especially red pigments used in this study were significantly degraded. The second part of the study collected littered HDPE plastic containers from a remote South African beach and analysed their condition as a function of the given manufacturing date stamp.\nL241: Most items were black or white and samples up to 45 years old were found with relatively little environmental degradation other than mild abrasion. It appears that carbon and titanium dioxide colourants protect the HDPE polymer from photolytic degradation.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn37view5 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0014305781900501\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n"
